{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput"]]},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures"},"abstract":[{"text":"Three- and four-finger strokes on the glass, for the Mac: which stroke is a gesture, and which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"gesture it is. Each input surface feeds one of these with every direct touch, through its stroke","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"observer. The counts below say three; with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chordFingers"},{"type":"text","text":" 4 read four."}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Gestures and zoom","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/SystemGesture","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/SystemGestureResolver","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/GestureShortcuts","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/ZoomStep","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/PinchStepper"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Gestures-and-zoom"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/init(chordFingers:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers"},{"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/armed","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/chordFingers","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/silent"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/cancelled(_:)","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/down(_:at:time:holding:)","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/moved(_:to:time:)","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/otherTouch()","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/up(_:at:time:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods"},{"title":"Enumerations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/Gesture","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/Output"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Enumerations"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TrackpadGestures"}],"title":"TrackpadGestures","roleHeading":"Structure","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TrackpadGestures"}],"role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"HeadwireInput"}],"externalID":"s:13HeadwireInput16TrackpadGesturesV"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TrackpadGestures","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A stroke runs from its first touch down to its last touch up. It goes ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"silent"}]},{"text":" once three fingers","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are down, before any finger has moved ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chordTravel"},{"text":" from where it landed and while no button the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"surface pressed is held (the trackpad’s press-and-hold drag), however slowly they came down and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whatever else rests on the glass. From then until the next stroke’s first touch the surfaces send","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing for it, no pointer motion, click, button or scroll (a tap’s action runs after its touch","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"has ended, so silence outlasts the last lift). A two-finger scroll that a third finger joins after","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"moving is never silent and goes on as it always did; a stroke that never has three fingers down is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"never silent, so one- and two-finger strokes are exactly what they were.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A silent stroke is ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"armed"}]},{"text":", one that can become a gesture, when the three fingers that landed last","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"came down within ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chordWindow"},{"text":" of each other, before any finger moved ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chordTravel"},{"text":", with no button","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"held, no touch of the stroke cancelled and at most four fingers down. So a thumb resting on the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"glass before neither keeps three fingers from arming nor becomes one of them; three fingers placed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"slowly are silent and decide nothing.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The decision comes at the first lift of one of those three (another finger lifting only leaves the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stroke), from their centroid’s net travel since arming, and their spread. A swipe when the centroid"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"travelled "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swipeDistance"},{"type":"text","text":" (or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flickDistance"},{"type":"text","text":" while moving at "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flickSpeed"},{"type":"text","text":" over the last"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flickWindow"},{"type":"text","text":"), one axis beats the other by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"axisRatio"},{"type":"text","text":", and the fingers moved together: each of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the three at least "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swipeShare"},{"type":"text","text":" of the centroid’s way along the swipe, and no other finger that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"moved ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chordTravel"},{"type":"text","text":" or more) that share or more against it. In a pinch or a spread some digit"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"moves against the others, however far the centroid goes (a thumb-led pinch drags it along with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the thumb). Else a pinch or a spread when the mean distance from the centroid changed by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pinchRatio"},{"type":"text","text":", of the three and every other finger that moved (a thumb pinching with three"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fingers); else nothing. At most one decision per stroke; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fingers"},{"type":"text","text":" counts the three and the other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fingers that moved, 4 at most. A fifth finger down leaves the stroke silent and deciding nothing;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"touches the system cancels decide nothing. So a swipe taken back before the lift does nothing, as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on a Mac, and a four-finger stroke that iPadOS takes for itself (its touches cancelled) never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reaches the Mac."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pure: Foundation and CoreGraphics only, covered by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackpadGesturesTests"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Deterministic: the same touches give the same outputs. Main thread, as the touches come."}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/headwireinput\/trackpadgestures"]}],"references":{"doc://HeadwireInput/documentation/HeadwireInput/TrackpadGestures":{"title":"TrackpadGestures","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TrackpadGestures"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Three- and four-finger strokes on the glass, for the Mac: which stroke is a gesture, and which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"gesture it is. Each input surface feeds one of these with every direct touch, through its stroke","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"observer. The counts below say three; with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chordFingers"},{"text":" 4 read four.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TrackpadGestures"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/headwireinput\/trackpadgestures"},"doc://HeadwireInput/documentation/HeadwireInput/TrackpadGestures/chordFingers":{"url":"\/documentation\/headwireinput\/trackpadgestures\/chordfingers","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The fingers that silence and arm a stroke."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/chordFingers","title":"chordFingers","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"chordFingers","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://HeadwireInput/documentation/HeadwireInput/GestureShortcuts":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The keystroke that triggers each system action on one Mac.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/headwireinput\/gestureshortcuts","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/GestureShortcuts","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"GestureShortcuts","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GestureShortcuts","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"GestureShortcuts","kind":"symbol"},"doc://HeadwireInput/documentation/HeadwireInput/TrackpadGestures/otherTouch()":{"url":"\/documentation\/headwireinput\/trackpadgestures\/othertouch()","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A touch that is not a finger (a Pencil, the iPad’s own trackpad or mouse) lands. It is never","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"part of a stroke, but with no finger down it starts something new: the last stroke’s silence"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ends, so a Pencil on the portrait trackpad right after a gesture is not ignored."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/otherTouch()","title":"otherTouch()","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"otherTouch"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://HeadwireInput/documentation/HeadwireInput/TrackpadGestures/init(chordFingers:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a recogniser whose strokes go silent and arm at "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chordFingers"},{"type":"text","text":" fingers, 3 or 4."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"init(chordFingers:)","url":"\/documentation\/headwireinput\/trackpadgestures\/init(chordfingers:)","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"chordFingers","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/init(chordFingers:)"},"doc://HeadwireInput/documentation/HeadwireInput":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput","title":"HeadwireInput","url":"\/documentation\/headwireinput","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Input events from the iPad, the same whichever path carries them to the Mac.","type":"text"}]},"doc://HeadwireInput/documentation/HeadwireInput/TrackpadGestures/up(_:at:time:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"A finger lifts. The first lift of one of the three that armed the stroke decides: ","type":"text"},{"code":".gesture","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"most once a stroke. Any other finger lifting only leaves the stroke (where it lifted counts, if","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it moved).","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/headwireinput\/trackpadgestures\/up(_:at:time:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/up(_:at:time:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"up"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"at"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:@S@CGPoint","text":"CGPoint"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"time"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@NSTimeInterval","text":"TimeInterval"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifi